cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the encoder-crossover-190 released data and verification tooling, please cite this deposit."
type: dataset
title: "The small-encoder crossover is a prompted-baseline artefact: a fine-tuned encoder head loses to a fine-tuned 4B decision model by 0.33 and to a majority-class control"
abstract: >-
  Released data and verification tooling for the encoder-crossover-190 (EXP12)
  paper. This deposit is NOT the paper text and NOT the measurement harness:
  it ships the sealed 190-case decision fixture and its schema, the frozen
  per-arm result records the published numbers rest on, the pre-registered
  protocols, an independent second-labelling record, and the scripts that
  re-derive the published numbers from those stored records. It does not
  retrain an arm, re-render a model input, or re-run the evaluation pipeline.
authors:
  - family-names: "Kalugasala Moorthy"
    given-names: "Aswin Ram"
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
license-url: "https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0"
keywords:
  - "encoder-crossover-190"
  - "EXP12"
  - "typed single-label decision"
  - "released data"
  - "verification tooling"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23463945"
